      <div class="text">
        <h2>Case study: Arnhems Buiten Electricity Campus</h2>
        <p>A first deployment of MICROGRID is being developed at the Arnhems Buiten Electricity Campus. The project was awarded through the competitive European open call for the HEDGE-IoT ecoystem, recognising both the need for better tools in campus energy management and the strength of MICROGRID as a practical, scalable solution. This real-world setting, with multiple organisations, diverse energy assets, and increasing system complexity, provided the ideal environment to bring the platform into operation.</p>
        <p>A key part of this deployment is the integration with the HEDGE-IoT framework, which enables real-time data exchange across the campus energy ecosystem. Through this integration, MICROGRID continuously receives live data on energy usage, system status, and distributed energy resources. By leveraging semantic interoperability standards, data from different systems and organisations can be combined and interpreted consistently, ensuring flexibility as the campus evolves and new assets are added.</p>
        <p>Beyond its technical and organisational value, the project also generates strong visibility impact. The Arnhems Buiten Electricity Campus acts as a national showcase for innovation in the energy transition, regularly hosting policymakers, utilities, and technology developers. By presenting a visually engaging digital twin of the local grid, MICROGRID provides a clear and compelling way to communicate how digitalisation and semantic interoperability can make local energy systems more transparent and efficient. Together with campus partners, the demonstrator will be featured at regional and national energy events, reinforcing the position of both Arnhems Buiten and the HEDGE-IoT framework as leading examples of practical, interoperable innovation.</p>
        <p>In the longer term, the expected impact includes improved collaboration between operators and technology providers, greater public and stakeholder understanding of energy flows and constraints, and a strengthened market position for interoperable, standards-based visualisation tools. Impact will be measured through the demonstrator's use in operational decision-making, its presence at major industry showcases, interest from other campuses, and integration of its components into ongoing commercial and research initiatives.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

